  "response": "{\n  \"title\": \"Forward Deployed Engineer\",\n  \"company\": \"AiStudio\",\n  \"location\": null,\n  \"employment_type\": \"full-time\",\n  \"workplace_type\": null,\n  \"salary_original\": \"₹15L – ₹20L\",\n  \"salary_min\": 1500000,\n  \"salary_max\": 2000000,\n  \"salary_currency\": \"INR\",\n  \"description\": \"About AiStudio\\n\\nAiStudio is an AI consultancy that embeds engineers directly inside portfolio companies of leading private equity firms. We don't sell software from the sidelines, we deploy engineers into the businesses themselves to build and ship AI solutions that move real metrics: cost savings, automation, revenue. We work with PE firms and their portfolio companies, building production systems ranging from ML models replacing manual processes to internal tools powering firm-wide operations.\\n\\nThe Role: Forward Deployed Engineer\\n\\nAs an FDE, you'll be embedded directly with client teams to understand real business problems and ship working software against them. This isn't a research role and it isn't classic consulting. You'll be writing code, shipping to production, and owning outcomes end to end, from scoping a solution design to deploying something a client's team relies on daily.\\n\\nWhat you'll actually do:\\n\\nScope and design technical solutions for live business problems, often replacing manual or legacy processes with automated, ML-driven ones\\nBuild production tools end to end (data pipelines, backend architecture, automation) using modern stacks and AI APIs\\nWork directly with client stakeholders, translating ambiguous asks into shipped features\\nTake ownership of your workstream, from architecture decisions to deployment tradeoffs\\n\\nWhat we look for:\\n\\nStrong CS fundamentals and genuine comfort shipping production code, not just prototypes\\nAbility to work with ambiguity and talk directly to non-technical stakeholders\\nBias toward outcomes over process; you care whether the thing you built actually worked\",\n  \"posted_at\": null\n}",
